A||||3||DaveL||87 2.5 Idle Transition||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||12-11-2001||04:01 PM||||My 87 2.5 runs into a momentary idle problem whenever I take off cold in the AM it idles around 1000 in drive, When it starts to warm up, the idle will settle down to about 550-600 in drive. But when ever it starts to change from the cold running "mode" into the warm running mode, it hits a period where it seems to miss and chug for just a minute or so. Changed plugs and wires, fuel injector, fuel filter. What could be causing this?<BR>Also found that the previous owner drove it around for 2-3 years with no thermostat in it. Can this carbon up the motor?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||12-11-2001||08:33 PM||||Running without a t/stat can carbon up the engine. As for your idle concern, I would recommend you clean your IAC pintle and thottle plate.<P>Hope this helps.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-11-2001||09:04 PM||||I agree totally with PBJ on this one.  Use a good quality throttle body cleaner and spray the tb while varying the rpm...don't be afraid to tach it out a bit.  Remove the IAC valve and clean the pinacle on the end of it with same cleaner and spray the cleaner in the iac hole and eventually take a screwdriver and rag and spray it and twist the rag and driver to remove any stubborn carbon residue. <P>GTDude||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-11-2001||11:29 PM||||replace the MAT sensor.... dis notes in my cave...<P>Might also need a ECT sensor. 4cyl qrg in my cave<BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
